WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.078 --> 00:00:03.914
It's a good thing cats have nine lives.

2
00:00:03.915 --> 00:00:09.453
Because the kitty from the city was in deep trouble!

3
00:00:09.454 --> 00:00:13.256
"The Calamity Gang?" Cleo said.

4
00:00:13.257 --> 00:00:16.751
"Are they outlaws?"

5
00:00:16.752 --> 00:00:19.818
Fritzy bit his lip.

6
00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:23.850
"The meanest outlaws in the West!"

7
00:00:23.851 --> 00:00:26.259
Mayor Wayne nodded.

8
00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:30.084
"They're the reason we needed a new sheriff."

9
00:00:30.085 --> 00:00:35.147
It seemed like Cleo's good luck had run out.

10
00:00:35.148 --> 00:00:40.341
"I can't stop a gang of outlaws!" she thought.

11
00:00:40.342 --> 00:00:43.856
She looked at Mayor Wayne and Fritzy.

12
00:00:43.857 --> 00:00:47.110
"But I can't tell them that."

13
00:00:47.111 --> 00:00:52.561
Cleo puffed out her chest. "You can count on me."

14
00:00:52.562 --> 00:00:58.776
"Glad to hear it," Mayor Wayne said.

15
00:00:58.777 --> 00:01:05.876
He and Fritzy left.

16
00:01:05.877 --> 00:01:09.720
"I need to get out of this town!" Cleo thought.

17
00:01:09.721 --> 00:01:12.589
"There must be some money around."

18
00:01:12.590 --> 00:01:16.613
She looked through every drawer and cabinet.

19
00:01:16.614 --> 00:01:21.097
All she found was an old boot.

20
00:01:21.098 --> 00:01:25.087
Cleo sighed.

21
00:01:25.088 --> 00:01:32.643
"Maybe someone in this town has money I can steal."

22
00:01:32.644 --> 00:01:35.615
She opened the front door.

23
00:01:35.616 --> 00:01:39.091
A young owl stood in her way.

24
00:01:39.092 --> 00:01:42.084
"Howdy, miss! I'm Oswald!

25
00:01:42.085 --> 00:01:45.400
Are you the new sheriff?"

26
00:01:45.401 --> 00:01:48.643
"I sure am, kid," Cleo said.

27
00:01:48.644 --> 00:01:50.465
"But I'm busy right now.

28
00:01:50.466 --> 00:01:53.260
I need to check out the town."

29
00:01:53.261 --> 00:01:56.050
"Great!" Oswald said.

30
00:01:56.051 --> 00:02:02.294
"I'll show you around."

31
00:02:02.295 --> 00:02:08.902
Oswald showed Cleo almost every building in town.

32
00:02:08.903 --> 00:02:11.884
That kid sure could talk.

33
00:02:11.885 --> 00:02:14.591
But Cleo wasn't paying much attention.

34
00:02:14.592 --> 00:02:18.838
She was too busy looking at everyone.

35
00:02:18.839 --> 00:02:22.787
"I have to find someone with money," she thought.

36
00:02:22.788 --> 00:02:28.075
"But nobody here looks rich."

37
00:02:28.076 --> 00:02:31.247
"Here we are," Oswald said.

38
00:02:31.248 --> 00:02:35.882
"The Prickly Pear Saloon!"

39
00:02:35.883 --> 00:02:48.414
Cleo and Oswald went inside and sat down.

40
00:02:48.415 --> 00:02:54.378
A badger named Buster poured two glasses of cactus juice.

41
00:02:54.379 --> 00:02:58.034
Cleo took out her coins.

42
00:02:58.035 --> 00:03:01.113
"Oops," she thought.

43
00:03:01.114 --> 00:03:05.857
It wasn't enough to pay for the juice.

44
00:03:05.858 --> 00:03:10.994
"I'm sorry," she said. "But I don't have—"

45
00:03:10.995 --> 00:03:14.385
"I'll pay for that," someone said.

46
00:03:14.386 --> 00:03:16.337
Cleo looked up.

47
00:03:16.338 --> 00:03:22.026
A fox stood nearby.

48
00:03:22.027 --> 00:03:27.633
She wore a long dress with a torn hem.

49
00:03:27.634 --> 00:03:31.460
"Miss Annie!" Oswald grinned.

50
00:03:31.461 --> 00:03:34.976
"Sheriff Cleo, Miss Annie is my teacher!"

51
00:03:34.977 --> 00:03:39.871
Annie smiled. "You must be our new sheriff."

52
00:03:39.872 --> 00:03:43.765
"My name's Cleo. But you don't have to—"

53
00:03:43.766 --> 00:03:46.260
Annie held up a paw.

54
00:03:46.261 --> 00:03:50.306
"In Prickly Pear we help each other out."

55
00:03:50.307 --> 00:03:53.272
Cleo couldn't believe it.

56
00:03:53.273 --> 00:03:56.369
"Annie seems poor," she thought.

57
00:03:56.370 --> 00:04:04.859
"But she's helping me anyway."

58
00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:09.942
Early the next morning, the train chugged along.

59
00:04:09.943 --> 00:04:14.277
Roscoe couldn't sleep.

60
00:04:14.278 --> 00:04:17.424
He was still mad.

61
00:04:17.425 --> 00:04:22.590
"If I ever see Cleo again, I'll throw her in jail!" he thought.

62
00:04:22.591 --> 00:04:24.298
"She's the worst—"

63
00:04:24.299 --> 00:04:25.842
"Hee-ya!"

64
00:04:25.843 --> 00:04:28.311
Roscoe looked out the window.

65
00:04:28.312 --> 00:04:35.247
Riders on horseback raced alongside the train.

66
00:04:35.248 --> 00:04:45.851
"Oh no!" Roscoe said. "Bandits!"

